    <File_Area_Observational>
        <File>
            <file_name>ca05_mvic_cube.fit</file_name>
            <comment>
                This file is the highest spatial resolution MVIC color observation of     
                Arrokoth designated as CA05, which was obtained on 2019 January 1         
                between 5:12:44 and 5:14:34 UTC (coordinated universal time). During      
                this observation period the spacecraft-center to target-center distance   
                decreased from 18,080 to 16,681 km, giving an image scale of the          
                observation between 330 and 362 meters per pixel. Over the observation    
                period the phase varied from 15.08 to 15.70 degrees.                      
                
                The color filters are identified as 'BLUE' (400-550 nm),                  
                'RED' (540-700 nm), 'NIR' (780-975 nm) and 'CH4' (860-910 nm)
            </comment>
        </File>
